 ### 3.3.4. Not yet implemented
 
-- **FR1–FR2** lack backend brand/user provisioning, account lifecycle management, per-user location and machine grants, complete asset history and time-limited pricing campaigns.
-- **FR3–FR4** lack live payment/refund providers and external reconciliation. Duplicate signed webhook handling remains unverified by IT-09. A rejection or timeout can reach the correct order state, but durable incident routing is missing in IT-02 and IT-04. The interlock scenario still lacks the required machine status update and alert evidence in IT-03.
-- **FR4–FR6** lack production MQTT security, complete device identity/revocation checks, an elapsed-time `UNSTABLE` rule, persisted telemetry/event history, and durable buffering and replay. Inventory intake, refill and adjustment lack a server-side workflow. Diagnostic consumption, low-stock alert generation and sensor reconciliation remain open.
-- **FR7–FR8** lack server-side alert delivery and escalation, automatic incident-to-ticket creation, and maintenance ticket, checklist and diagnostic closure workflows.
-- **FR9–FR10** lack database-backed tenant reporting and historical operational metrics, comprehensive backend audit coverage, audit search and an end-to-end trace including the incident. Browser demo data and exports establish UI behaviour. Physical dispensing and sensor accuracy remain unverified.
+- **Frontend to backend.** No screen calls the API. This is the single largest
+  gap and it touches every requirement group: the portal demonstrates the
+  interaction design of Section 2.10 against browser storage, while the
+  equivalent server-side operation exists and is tested separately. Joining them
+  is implementation work rather than design work, and `docs/api-contract.md` is
+  what it would follow.
+- **FR1–FR2** lack per-user location and machine grants, complete configuration
+  and asset history, and time-limited pricing campaigns.
+- **FR3–FR4** lack live payment and refund providers and external reconciliation.
+  Duplicate signed webhook handling is recorded as a failure in IT-09 and is not
+  yet re-verified. Production MQTT transport security, device identity
+  revocation and an elapsed-time `UNSTABLE` rule remain open.
+- **FR5–FR6** lack persisted telemetry and event history for trend analysis,
+  durable buffering and replay across a broker disconnect, diagnostic
+  consumption accounting, and reconciliation of measured volume against the
+  sensor reading.
+- **FR7–FR8** lack outbound alert delivery and escalation by elapsed time:
+  alerts are raised, deduplicated and escalated into a ticket in the database,
+  but nothing leaves the system, and the `notifications` table is created and
+  unused. Scheduled preventive maintenance remains open.
+- **FR9** lacks server-side tenant-scoped reporting and historical operational
+  metrics. The code exists on an unmerged branch.
+- **FR10** lacks a single end-to-end trace joining an order, its command, its
+  alert and its maintenance ticket.
+- **Hardware.** Physical dispensing, dosage accuracy and sensor calibration are
+  unverified: the device tier is a simulator, and no part of this project ran
+  against a real kiosk.
 
 These gaps are carried forward to [Section 4.2, Limitations](<04.Conclusion.md#42-limitations>).
 
